    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31392" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nŭma</span></b> , ae, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a Roman proper
			name</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Numa
			Pompilius, <i>the second king of Rome</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 1, 18
				sq.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Rep. 2, 13, 25</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2, 18,
				33</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. F. 2, 69</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. ib. 3,
				305</span></i> sqq.; Juv 3, 16; 8, 156 al.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Numa Marcius (Martius), <i>a Sabine, a friend of the former and
			high-priest</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 1, 20</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 6,
			11</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
